  "releaseNotes": "Release candidate turning \"the export is not downloadable yet\" into a catchable failure.\n\nHighlights:\n- DownloadExportAsync now raises FiskalyExportNotReadyException instead of a bare InvalidOperationException.\n  The old type sat outside the FiskalyException hierarchy every caller catches, so an ordinary race - the\n  state is read here, immediately before the download, and the export finishes in between - escaped as an\n  unhandled exception and surfaced as an HTTP 500 in consuming applications\n- the exception carries State, ExportId and the provider's ExceptionCode, plus IsTransient, so a caller can\n  tell the two cases apart: PENDING/WORKING becomes downloadable on its own and is worth polling, ERROR never\n  does and polling it is an infinite wait\n- source-compatible for anyone who catches FiskalyException; only code that catches InvalidOperationException\n  specifically around a download needs to change",
